#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:10
#: f3c9503f060445438d43262781100ad0
msgid ""
"This troubleshoot applies to the non-default kernel choice described in "
"the :ref:`Managing VM docs <user/advanced-topics/managing-vm-kernels:using "
"kernel installed in the vm>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:12
#: cdbe1d6f45fa49e0aa5020036eb70c8f
msgid ""
"In case of problems, you can access the VM console using ``qvm-console-"
"dispvm VMNAME`` in dom0, then access the GRUB menu. You need to call it just "
"after starting the VM (until ``GRUB_TIMEOUT`` expires); for example, in a "
"separate dom0 terminal window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:14
#: ace7e7c4764f480e9fecf2c2ab5d7f40
msgid ""
"In any case you can later access the VM’s logs (especially the VM console "
"log ``/var/log/xen/console/guest-VMNAME.log``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:16
#: ef888d5e1ec3461c80eb3ff550aae684
msgid ""
"You can always set the kernel back to some dom0-provided value to fix a VM "
"kernel installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:19
#: eb7c926cdb5046dc86b927b5cf4e2b3e
msgid "Qubes starts, but no VMs load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:22
#: bb1e307fcb404d13b3f470e4d06ce91a
msgid ""
"First, try to start a particular VM, check any failure message and direct "
"further steps based on that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/vm-troubleshooting.rst:24
#: afb9ee3eb9a34af3a5d2277031f91429
msgid ""
"This issue has been seen to occur if a dom0 update is interrupted halfway "
"through and/or a hard power off is done without shutting down Qubes, which "
"results in files getting corrupted."
msgstr ""

